OL,4,G1930FRadio 3 in Concert
OL,5,     GThe London Philharmonic Orchestra
OL,6,     Gperforms Anna Thorvaldsdottir's
OL,7,     GCATAMORPHOSIS and Beethoven's 6th
OL,8,     GSymphony. Plus Bruch's Violin
OL,9,     GConcerto with Nikolaj Szeps-
OL,10,     GZnaider.
OL,11,G2145FThe Essay: Healing Musicians
OL,12,     GKate Kennedy meets principal
OL,13,     GFrench horn player Robin Graham
OL,14,     Gto learn what it means for a
OL,15,     Gmusician's relationship with
OL,16,     Gtheir instrument when injury
OL,17,     Gforces them to stop playing.
